{"type":"text","timestamp":1794564450382,"sessionID":"ses_e2ba44b7cffeY7DCkwAjaaon0M","part":{"id":"prt_1d46056840011vLUgOGfZBmOzh","sessionID":"ses_e2ba44b7cffeY7DCkwAjaaon0M","messageID":"msg_1d46042ab001RiggfpISSIjZX6","type":"text","text":"T004 is done and verified.\n\n**Files written**\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` — removed the compiled-route push block and the now-unused `renderCompiledRouteSummaryLine` import, and left a comment where the block was explaining that the head entry already carries the hub, command and policy while the route summary keeps string targets only.\n- `.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs` — the flag-off test now asserts `output.system.length` is 1, and `bounded flag selects the bounded line in the OpenCode transform` is renamed to `bounding leaves the OpenCode transform with the head entry alone`, drops its `renderHelpers` line and asserts one entry.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n$ node --check .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js\nnode-check-exit=0\n\n$ rg -c \"renderCompiledRouteSummaryLine|output.system.push\\(compiledLine\\)\" .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js\nscan1-exit=1            (no output: no match)\n\n$ rg -c \"compiledRouteSummary\" .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js\n3\n\n$ node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs\nℹ tests 42\nℹ pass 42\nℹ fail 0\n\n$ (ADV) env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/system-skill-advisor-plugin.vitest.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  97 passed (97)\n\n$ node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check\n[runtime-mirror-sync] PASS: 256 mirrors across 10 trees are in sync.\nSRM-exit=0\n\n$ readlink .skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/opencode/system-skill-advisor.js\n../../../../.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js\n```\n\n`git status --short -- .opencode/plugins` lists only those two modified files.\n\n**One deviation, recorded:** the task says to replace the renamed test's two `output.system[1]` assertions with `assert.equal(output.system.length, 1)`. I wrote that assertion once rather than twice, since a duplicate identical assertion pins nothing and reads as an editing artifact. All other instructions were followed literally.\n\n**Not done:** the `- [ ] T004` checkbox in `tasks.md` is deliberately left unticked, and nothing else was touched.\n\n**Operator's to do:** review the diff above and tick T004.","time":{"start":1794564445828,"end":1794564450382}}}
